# MemberCallSubstitution's DERIVED completeness gate. A Kotlin-spelled member on a @ClrTypeAlias'd interface owner
# that the resolved BCL type does not declare must be a compile-time routing MISS, naming owner.member — never a
# call nothing can link, and never (as before #400) a runtime GetType().GetMethod(name).Invoke lookup.
#
# Valid Kotlin source cannot witness this: every Kotlin collection member without a physical slot is routed, which
# is exactly why the rule needs a synthetic document to keep it from being silently defeated.
unrouted Kotlin member 'kotlin.collections.MutableCollection.sortAll'
declares no 'sortAll'
must be routed to a physical implementation
